	(text "EoS KE16Z Board, rev A. Designed by Kartikeydheer Srivastava. Fits Uno R3 shields; 3.3 V I/O.\nCopyright (c) 2026 Kartikeydheer Srivastava. All rights reserved; see LICENSE.txt.\nValues from NXP KE1xZP48M48SF0 (data sheet) and KE1xZP48M48SF0RM, AN3208, AN1706, ST AN2867;\nSilicon Labs CP2102N Rev. 1.5, Diodes DS37274 (AP7361C), Nexperia PMEG6010CEH, Littelfuse, Wurth, AOS.\nFirmware: run the 8 MHz oscillator in low-power mode (HGO = 0): high-gain mode would\noverdrive the crystal (AN3208 Eqn. 1), and RF must not be fitted (DS Table 40 note 3)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260 360 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3d60827d-0e36-5064-a49d-75985d96be14")
	)
	(text "Power: USB-C VBUS through F1 and D1 to the 5 V rail (LDO, RGB LED, 5V pin);\nD1 keeps a shield's 5 V off the host. The CP2102N runs from 3.3 V and senses VBUS\n(R6, R7); R5 bleeds D1's leakage off VBUS, so it connects only with a host present."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 400 372 0)
